  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its siting and massing, would result in the loss of the characteristic first-floor separation between properties and would erode the established spacing and rhythm of development along Manor Drive North. The two-storey side extension, being flush with the shared boundary at first-floor level, would create a terracing effect that is uncharacteristic of the prevailing pattern of semi-detached dwellings and would cause unacceptable harm to the character and appearance of the host dwelling and the surrounding area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Paragraph 135 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), Policy DM10 of the Council's Core Strategy (2012) and the guidance contained within the Council's Residential Design SPD (2013)."
